    {"role": "user", "content": "Kan jy my help met hierdie vraag? $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ indien $y = 2x + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x}}$. Ek weet nie eintlik waar om te begin nie."},
    {"role": "assistant", "reasoning": "Learner is blank_stuck and asks for help. Fast-track mode: give one small diagnostic question about rewriting the radical as a power, then wait. [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"sqrt(4x)\") -> 2*sqrt(x)]", "content": "Geen probleem nie! Kom ons breek dit stap vir stap af.\n\nEers, kan jy $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x}}$ herskryf met behulp van negatiewe eksponente? (Onthou: $\\sqrt{x} = x^{1/2}$ en $\\frac{1}{x^n} = x^{-n}$.)\n\nWat dink jy die uitdrukking sou lyk?"}
  ],
  "meta": {
    "strategy_used": "step_walkthrough",
    "final_answer": "2 - \\frac{1}{4}x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}",
    "verify_code": "import sympy as sp\nx = sp.symbols('x')\ny = 2*x + 1/sp.sqrt(4*x)\nprint(sp.diff(y, x))",
    "techniques": ["rewrite_radical_as_power", "differentiate_term_by_term"]
  }
}

